# State Performance (Telegram-level)

## Per-channel state isolation (MessageStore)

```kotlin
// CRITICAL — MessageStore uses ConcurrentHashMap, NOT a global Map StateFlow
private val channels = ConcurrentHashMap<Long, MutableStateFlow<ChannelState>>()

fun getChannelFlow(channelId: Long): StateFlow<ChannelState> =
    getOrCreate(channelId).asStateFlow()
```

Mutating channel A does NOT emit to channel B subscribers. This eliminates the N-channel fan-out problem.

## ViewModel: flatMapLatest, NOT double-stateIn

```kotlin
// BAD — subscribes to entire Map<Long, List>, re-evaluates on every channel's update
val uiState = combine(
    messageStore.channelMessages,  // global map — emits on ANY channel change
    _channelId, ...
) { allMessages, channelId, ... -> allMessages[channelId] }

// GOOD — only subscribes to the active channel's flow
val uiState = _channelId.flatMapLatest { channelId ->
    if (channelId == null) return@flatMapLatest flowOf(ChatUiState.Loading)
    combine(
        messageStore.getChannelFlow(channelId),
        _isLoadingMore
    ) { channelState, isLoadingMore -> ... }
}.stateIn(viewModelScope, ...)
```

## Cap message list per channel

```kotlin
private const val MAX_MESSAGES_PER_CHANNEL = 200

fun addNewMessage(entity: MessageEntity) {
    flow.update { state ->
        val combined = state.messages + entity
        val trimmed = if (combined.size > MAX_MESSAGES_PER_CHANNEL)
            combined.drop(combined.size - MAX_MESSAGES_PER_CHANNEL)
        else combined
        state.copy(messages = trimmed)
    }
}
```

## Batch DAO writes (DirectStore presence)

```kotlin
// BAD — N coroutines launched inside _state.update
_directs.update { current ->
    current.map { dm ->
        if (dm.channelId in onlineUserIds) {
            appScope.launch { dao.updateOnlineStatus(dm.channelId, true) }  // BAD
            dm.copy(isOnline = true)
        } else dm
    }
}

// GOOD — collect IDs, single batch write after state update
val changedOnline = mutableListOf<Long>()
_directs.update { current ->
    current.map { dm ->
        if (dm.channelId in onlineUserIds && !dm.isOnline) {
            changedOnline.add(dm.channelId)
            dm.copy(isOnline = true)
        } else dm
    }
}
appScope.launch { changedOnline.forEach { dao.updateOnlineStatus(it, true) } }
```

## Use Long/Int keys, not String

Proto IDs are `Long`. Keep them as `Long` everywhere — no `.toString()` conversions for comparisons or map keys.

## Pre-parse at mapping boundary

Parse content in `toMessageEntity()` / `toDirectMessage()`, cached Regex in `util/ContentParser.kt`:

```kotlin
// All parsing uses shared cached Regex from ContentParser.kt
val content = remember(msg.content) { parseContentText(msg.content) }
val time = remember(msg.timestampSeconds) { formatRelativeTime(msg.timestampSeconds) }
```
